WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.802
Validation is not optional. State the row grain.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:08.732
Compare totals when the measure is additive.

00:00:08.732 --> 00:00:12.017
Check whether NULL values were preserved or filtered intentionally.

00:00:12.017 --> 00:00:17.492
Inspect the plan for unnecessary scans or shuffles.

00:00:17.492 --> 00:00:23.792
A pipeline is stronger when the result is both correct and explainable.

00:00:23.792 --> 00:00:32.027
Connect this idea to a retail pipeline aggregating high-volume sales data across partitions.

00:00:32.027 --> 00:00:37.062
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.062 --> 00:00:45.702
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.702 --> 00:00:51.197
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.197 --> 00:00:59.040
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
